minimum values at:\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi \n$$\n\nSince the domain $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi $ is one period, and we have already found one minimum value in this period, we conclude that $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is the only solution." 13194139533913 true] [17592186092811 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533913 true] [17592186092811 1145 "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ \n\nAs this is a quadrantal angle, to find the remaining solutions we use our knowledge of the sine function. We know that the sine function has its  minimum values at:\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi \n$$\n\nSince the domain $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi $ is one period, and we have already found one minimum value in this period, we conclude that $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is the only solution." 13194139533913 true] [17592186265317 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265318 13194139533913 true] [17592186265317 1089 "q-120835" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265317 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533913 true] [17592186265317 1100 "Calculate, in degrees, rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{5}{8}$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265317 1113 #uuid "b24174ad-9291-5093-8bdb-f1435a702636" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265317 1145 "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{5}{8})=38.682{…}^{∘}≈{38.68}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${38.68}^{∘}$ lies inside the range, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={38.68}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={38.68}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={38.68}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951962/assets/12b17e3994be5e45af3aca185b22618dd0ec7288fba18a4131387783323247a0.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{38.68}^{∘} \\\\  & ={141.32}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions (rounded to the nearest integer) are $x={39}^{∘},{141}^{∘}.$" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265318 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265319 13194139533913 true] [17592186265318 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265320 13194139533913 true] [17592186265318 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265321 13194139533913 true] [17592186265318 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265322 13194139533913 true] [17592186265318 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265323 13194139533913 true] [17592186265318 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533913 true] [17592186265318 1041 "selection" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265318 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265319 13194139533913 true] [17592186265318 1110 #uuid "a5d01cbc-623a-5367-b7ea-1056e8ee04b4" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265319 1034 "x={39}^{∘},{141}^{∘}" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265319 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533913 true] [17592186265319 1111 #uuid "fa8977ac-e0bd-5261-8984-7a0637b2fa3c" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265320 1034 "x={59}^{∘},{121}^{∘}" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265320 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533913 true] [17592186265320 1111 #uuid "10d94569-9f19-5933-92b1-c0077a8f02eb" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265321 1034 "x={33}^{∘},{147}^{∘}" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265321 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533913 true] [17592186265321 1111 #uuid "f3992956-1191-5178-be27-96a3227ea006" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265322 1034 "x={41}^{∘},{139}^{∘}" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265322 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533913 true] [17592186265322 1111 #uuid "7bc103b4-a80a-51db-b98d-ee38391d5f7e" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265323 1034 "x={49}^{∘},{131}^{∘}" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265323 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533913 true] [17592186265323 1111 #uuid "fd650180-c584-552e-983f-b1e86bd1d806" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265324 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265325 13194139533913 true] [17592186265324 1089 "q-17495" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265324 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533913 true] [17592186265324 1100 "Calculate, in degrees, rounded to the nearest integer, the solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{11}{13}$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x\\le {180}^{∘}.$" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265324 1113 #uuid "1854b83d-f26f-59a0-b8ab-54decd251347" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265324 1145 "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{11}{13})=-57.795\\,772{…}^{∘}≈-{57.796}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-{57.796}^{∘}$ lies inside the range, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-{57.796}^{∘}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={57.796}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={57.796}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951962/assets/f204faa6327d057dbea5de66f2c6ffca0a9982c299d1e4278dbc6514ddf016df.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={180}^{∘}+{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}+{57.796}^{∘} \\\\  & ={237.796}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get the second solution ${x}_{2}$ that's within the given domain, we simply subtract ${360}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=X-{360}^{∘}={237.796}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}=-{122.204}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions (rounded to the nearest integer) are $x=-{122}^{∘},-{58}^{∘}.$" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265325 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265326 13194139533913 true] [1759