e{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{2},$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}} $,\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}$.$" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265331 1113 #uuid "5395407a-550d-531d-be2e-5a1a73b82301" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265331 1145 "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951962/assets/b7b581dc39ba057033703c3549a721679d1d063267e13b65c73a9b9fcd66f1e6.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get the second solution ${x}_{2}$ that's within the given domain, we simply subtract $2\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=X-2\\pi  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}-2\\pi =-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the solutions are \n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{5\\pi }{6},\\,x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\n$$" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265332 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265333 13194139533913 true] [17592186265332 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265334 13194139533913 true] [17592186265332 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533913 true] [17592186265332 1041 "field-1" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265332 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265334 13194139533913 true] [17592186265332 1110 #uuid "24d0a9c7-d834-5952-86e2-fddffe662513" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265333 1034 "\\frac{5\\pi}{6}" 13194139533913 true] [1