9" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265378 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533913 true] [17592186265378 1100 "Find the exact solution to the equation  $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3=0$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi .$ Give your answer in radians.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265378 1113 #uuid "cc58faac-ba81-5140-b800-d51ae6619aa6" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265378 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-3 & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =3 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(1)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ \n\nAs this is a quadrantal angle, to find the remaining solutions, we use our knowledge of the sine function. We know that the sine function has its maximum values at:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi \n$$\n\nSince the domain $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi $ is one period, and we have already found one maximum value in this period, we conclude that $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is the only solution." 13194139533913 true] [17592186265379 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265380 13194139533913 true] [17592186265379 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265381 13194139533913 true] [17592186265379 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533913 true] [17592186265379 1041 "field-1" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265379 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265381 13194139533913 true] [17592186265379 1110 #uuid "3b027324-1561-50d1-8084-19ff62b1720c" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265380 1034 "-\\frac{\\pi}{2}" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265380 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533913 true] [17592186265380 1111 #uuid "0aaefa1c-7b81-5b24-909d-d8be01abf5f6" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265381 1034 "\\frac{\\pi}{2}" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265381 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533913 true] [17592186265381 1111 #uuid "bad0e88f-80b3-54da-9