51962/assets/0716b8ab50e525f453ae8bc690d404a150f2da98f0a90b6c8856ae9925e7c515.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3},\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{x}_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}\\cdot \\frac{4\\pi }{3}=\\frac{20{\\pi }^{2}}{9}.\n$$" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265397 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265398 13194139533913 true] [17592186265397 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265399 13194139533913 true] [17592186265397 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265400 13194139533913 true] [17592186265397 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265401 13194139533913 true] [17592186265397 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265402 13194139533913 true] [17592186265397 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533913 true] [17592186265397 1041 "selection" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265397 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265401 13194139533913 true] [17592186265397 1110 #uuid "4184cc1c-6b9c-510d-847e-5d8d41baec28" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265398 1034 "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265398 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533913 true] [17592186265398 1111 #uuid "9af43ed6-6ed6-5d2e-8bb0-a63019e4c4d0" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265399 1034 "\\frac{10{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265399 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533913 true] [17592186265399 1111 #uuid "6e406ad8-6993-5f37-b1b0-4b56ccc50379" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265400 1034 "\\frac{8{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265400 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533913 true] [17592186265400 1111 #uuid "00f3e839-c938-5d78-84d4-a99b51dc0078" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265401 1034 "\\frac{20{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265401 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533913 true] [17592186265401 1111 #uuid "5b5b71e2-dab5-5a17-8fc4-92cbf972fd06" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265402 1034 "\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265402 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533913 true] [17592186265402 1111 #uuid "f34b7938-c0b1-5402-a6a8-3e82d975be90" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265403 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265404 13194139533913 true] [17592186265403 1089 "q-8435" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265403 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533913 true] [17592186265403 1100 "Find the solutions to the equation $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2=0$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265403 1113 #uuid "5dc2b789-e2f1-573b-a8c7-91ecf7b0de81" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265403 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2 & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-2 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is not in the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ To get the first solution that's within the required domain, we need to find an angle that's coterminal with $-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ To do this, we simply add $2\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2\\pi =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nAs this is a quadrantal angle, to find the remaining solutions we use our knowledge of the sine function. We know that the sine function has its minimum values at:\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi \n$$\n\nSince the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi $ is one period, and we have already found one minimum value in this period, we conclude that $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is the only solution." 13194139533913 true] [17592186265404 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265405 13194139533913 true] [17592186265404 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265406 13194139533913 true] [17592186265404 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265407 13194139533913 true] [17592186265404 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265408 13194139533913 true] 