 isolating $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\sqrt{2} & =0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951962/assets/269d503189ab1027c3d8028542ef0c6a0e2f146aef0f7916691428866ce1b894.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{4}=\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{16}.\n$$" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265411 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265412 13194139533913 true] [17592186265411 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265413 13194139533913 true] [17592186265411 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265414 13194139533913 true] [17592186265411 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265415 13194139533913 true] [17592186265411 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265416 13194139533913 true] [17592186265411 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533913 true] [17592186265411 1041 "selection" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265411 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265416 13194139533913 true] [17592186265411 1110 #uuid "63a69bd0-ac4e-5632-b30b-bb335315fa7c" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265412 1034 "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{18}" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265412 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533913 true] [17592186265412 1111 #uuid "a1594908-f00c-5217-be7d-a7a74d1f71c5" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265413 1034 "-\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{16}" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265413 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533913 true] [17592186265413 1111 #uuid "381ed357-d22d-5fc8-bc14-b4a9d49c21a9" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265414 1034 "\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265414 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533913 true] [17592186265414 1111 #uuid "aeffb562-9114-543a-bbe2-1ca914dd8550" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265415 1034 "\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{9}" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265415 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533913 true] [17592186265415 1111 #uuid "61532bd5-d33e-5e7a-9cb2-1c9d54fd5ac1" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265416 1034 "\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{16}" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265416 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533913 true] [17592186265416 1111 #uuid "01519aff-8466-512f-b32f-c9ab38441858" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265417 1017 #edb/ref 17592186265418 13194139533913 true] [17592186265417 1089 "q-8577" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265417 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533913 true] [17592186265417 1100 "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions of the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{6}$ for $-\\pi <x\\le \\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to $1$ decimal place?" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265417 1113 #uuid "94f21909-0674-569b-9e74-b7afb787ec1c" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265417 1145 "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{6})=-0.167\\,448…≈-0.167\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-0.167$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=-0.167\\,4.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the fourth quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=0.167\\,4.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=0.167\\,4.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13951962/assets/f6f08d799cd2d2e80494d94cc3b18a61f73227b88b25d79c926d65e161d4ce3a.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $3$rd quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +0.167\\,4 \\\\  & ≈3.309\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get the second solution ${x}_{2}$ that's within the given domain, we simply subtract $2\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=X-2\\pi  & ≈3.309-2\\pi ≈-2.974\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=(-0.167\\,4)\\cdot (-2.974\\,2)≈0.5,\n$$\n\nrounded to $1$ decimal place." 13194139533913 true] [17592186265418 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265419 13194139533913 true] [17592186265418 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265420 13194139533913 true] [17592186265418 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265421 13194139533913 true] [17592186265418 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265422 13194139533913 true] [17592186265418 1000 #edb/ref 17592186265423 13194139533913 true] [17592186265418 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533913 true] [17592186265418 1041 "selection" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265418 1104 #edb/ref 17592186265423 13194139533913 true] [17592186265418 1110 #uuid "c8d0296e-d835-500c-b67b-42fc5db69ee3" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265419 1034 "0.6" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265419 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533913 true] [17592186265419 1111 #uuid "b5f88483-fb58-5083-995b-e2c47fb0d899" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265420 1034 "0.2" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265420 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533913 true] [17592186265420 1111 #uuid "693dc3f6-d8a0-57f3-ac6c-29672825f04e" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265421 1034 "0.7" 13194139533913 true] [17592186265421 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533913 true] [17592186265421 1111 #uui